course: dictionary
lesson: 6442
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so look at the words around them. «Astronauts could not see the Great Wall with the naked eye (without a telescope) from orbit.» The brackets tell you what the phrase means: the naked eye means your own eyes, with no telescope or other tool.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. A naked flame is an open flame with nothing covering it, and it is dangerous near gas. A naked light bulb has no lampshade. Naked can also mean plain and obvious, as in the naked truth.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. «The Great Wall cannot be seen with the naked eye from space, because it is narrow.» Swap in "with your own eyes, without a tool" and the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Naked means without clothes on, or without the usual cover.
fact: «The naked eye» means your eyes alone, with no telescope or microscope.
fact: «A naked flame» means an open flame, which is dangerous near gas.
fact: «The naked truth» means the plain, obvious truth.
fact: The Great Wall of China is very long but narrow, so it is very hard to see with the naked eye from space.
exercise: «The Great Wall cannot be seen with the naked eye from space.» What does «with the naked eye» mean? | *Without any tool, using only your eyes | With a telescope | With a camera on a rocket | In the dark
exercise: Mia reads, «Keep away from the naked flame near the gas.» What is dangerous? | A candle in a jar | *An open flame with nothing covering it | The gas cooker when it is switched off | A torch
exercise: «The Great Wall is very long but only about as wide as a road.» Why can it not be seen from the Moon with the naked eye? | *Because it is narrow, like a road | Because the Moon is too bright | Because it is covered in trees | Because it is very short
test: «Astronauts could not see the Great Wall with the naked eye (without a telescope) from orbit.» What does naked eye mean here? | *Your eyes alone, with no tool | A telescope | An eye covered by a bandage | A pair of binoculars
test: Ben says «the naked truth» means a hidden truth. What does it really mean? | *The plain, obvious truth | A secret truth | A truth told in a song | A made-up story
exam: Lily reads, «A naked flame is dangerous near gas.» What is a naked flame? | *A flame with no cover, open to the air | A flame made of gas | A tiny flame in a lamp | A flame with a cover on it
